{
    "schema_version":  1,
    "purpose":  "Shared module-reachability differential corpus for the two independently owned resolvers. It exists because a whole-tree sweep is silent on any rule the repository never exercises: the tracked tree contains zero inline #[path] modules and zero ambiguous module pairs, so agreeing real-tree path sets prove nothing about either rule.",
    "rule":  "A cited evidence path must be a target root, or a source file reachable from a test-enabled target root by explicit mod, inline mod, or #[path] traversal, within the package that owns it.",
    "arbiter":  "cargo and rustc, executed against each fixture. Neither implementation is normative for reachability: every expectation below was produced by building or listing the fixture with the real toolchain, never written by hand or copied from either resolver.",
    "implementations":  [
                            {
                                "path":  "crates/claw-conformance/src/claims.rs",
                                "entry_point":  "CargoTestTargets"
                            },
                            {
                                "path":  "compat/upstream/validate.ps1",
                                "entry_point":  "Assert-EvidenceFileIsCompiled"
                            }
                        ],
